msgid "First, we use the Qiskit ``Statevector`` class to simulate the exact target values for our experiment. While the 22-qubit problem we're solving is tractable classically, the Qiskit statevector simulator will not scale to demos much larger than this one, and to scale up past 50 qubits or so, we would need to use inexact simulation techniques, such as [Pauli propagation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/pauli-prop). This 49-qubit experiment allows us to investigate combining error detection with error mitigation at larger scales while maintaining access to the ideal expectation values.\n"
msgstr "Una, ginagamit natin ang Qiskit ``Statevector`` class upang i-simulate ang eksaktong target values para sa ating eksperimento. Habang ang 22-qubit na problema na ating nilulutas ay tractable nang klasikal, hindi mag-i-scale ang Qiskit statevector simulator sa mga demo na mas malaki kaysa dito, at upang mag-scale nang lampas sa halos 50 qubits, kakailanganin nating gumamit ng inexact na mga simulation technique, tulad ng [Pauli propagation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/pauli-prop). Pinapayagan tayo ng 49-qubit na eksperimentong ito na siyasatin ang pagsasama ng error detection at error mitigation sa mas malaking sukat habang pinapanatili ang access sa ideal na expectation values.\n"

