msgstr "Magdagdag ng non-Markovian error checks sa circuit {#add-non-markovian-error-checks-to-the-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we add [non-Markovian error checks](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-mitigation/blob/main/docs/guides/postselection_with_non_markovian_error_checks.ipynb) to the circuit in order to protect against noise that isn't modeled in our learning protocol. These checks work by implementing a long-pulse bit-flip and ensuring the qubit correctly moved from one classical state to another. If both qubits on an edge fail the check, the sample is discarded. Non-Markovian error checks can be used at the beginning or end of the circuit (or both); here we use them only at the end. We also place checks on unused \"spectator\" qubits adjacent to the circuit, providing more coverage against the noise these checks are designed to detect.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, magdaragdag tayo ng [non-Markovian error checks](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-mitigation/blob/main/docs/guides/postselection_with_non_markovian_error_checks.ipynb) sa circuit upang maprotektahan laban sa noise na hindi na-model sa ating learning protocol. Gumagana ang mga check na ito sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatupad ng isang long-pulse bit-flip at pagtitiyak na tama ang paglipat ng qubit mula sa isang classical state patungo sa isa pa. Kung bigo sa check ang parehong qubit sa isang edge, itinatapon ang sample. Maaaring gamitin ang non-Markovian error checks sa simula o dulo ng circuit (o sa pareho); dito, ginagamit lamang natin ito sa dulo. Naglalagay rin tayo ng mga check sa hindi ginagamit na mga \"spectator\" qubit na katabi ng circuit, na nagbibigay ng mas malawak na saklaw laban sa noise na dinisenyo ng mga check na ito upang matukoy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember, similar to symmetry checks, this is also a form of postselection, so we need to ensure we are accounting for the drop in postselection rate when combining these techniques. Concretely, if $P(\\text{non-Markovian error}) = \\alpha$ and $P(\\text{symmetry error}) = \\beta$, then you need approximately $\\frac{1}{(1-\\alpha)(1-\\beta)}$ noisy samples to recover one logical sample.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan, katulad ng symmetry checks, isa rin itong anyo ng postselection, kaya kailangan nating tiyakin na isinasaalang-alang natin ang pagbaba sa postselection rate kapag pinagsama ang mga teknik na ito. Sa partikular, kung $P(\\text{non-Markovian error}) = \\alpha$ at $P(\\text{symmetry error}) = \\beta$, kakailanganin mo ng humigit-kumulang $\\frac{1}{(1-\\alpha)(1-\\beta)}$ na maingay na sample upang mabawi ang isang logical sample.\n"

