msgstr "Alamin ang gate at readout noise para sa 49-qubit na checked-Ising circuit {#learn-the-gate-and-readout-noise-for-the-49-qubit-checked-ising-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To mitigate the noise, we must model how the noise is affecting our entangling gates. Here we learn a Pauli-Lindblad noise model for each of the circuit's three unique entangling layers using [qiskit-noise-learning](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-noise-learning). Later, we will prune this noise model of error generators that are detectable by the symmetry checks and mitigate only the remaining noise channel with PEC. The map below shows the three learned layers on the QPU; each qubit is a wheel of its weight-1 X/Y/Z rates, and each coupler a 3×3 grid of the weight-2 Pauli rates on that pair. The $\\gamma$ value of $10$ implies a sampling overhead of $\\gamma^2=10^2=100$.\n"
msgstr "Upang bawasan ang noise, kailangan nating i-model kung paano nakakaapekto ang noise sa ating mga entangling gate. Dito, natututo tayo ng isang Pauli-Lindblad noise model para sa bawat isa sa tatlong natatanging entangling layer ng circuit gamit ang [qiskit-noise-learning](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-noise-learning). Sa susunod, ipu-prune natin ang noise model na ito ng mga error generator na madedeteksyunan ng symmetry checks at babawasan lamang ang natitirang noise channel gamit ang PEC. Ipinapakita ng mapa sa ibaba ang tatlong natutunang layer sa QPU; ang bawat qubit ay isang gulong ng kanyang weight-1 na X/Y/Z rates, at ang bawat coupler ay isang 3×3 na grid ng weight-2 na Pauli rates sa pares na iyon. Ang halagang $\\gamma$ na $10$ ay nagpapahiwatig ng sampling overhead na $\\gamma^2=10^2=100$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The readout (TREX) corrections come directly from the SPAM paths of the noise-learning fit. The stem plot below the QPU noise map shows the per-observable TREX rescale factors.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga readout (TREX) correction ay direktang nagmumula sa mga SPAM path ng noise-learning fit. Ipinapakita ng stem plot sa ibaba ng QPU noise map ang per-observable na TREX rescale factors.\n"

